module gunbc.plans.logical_work_realization

import std.dissolution { unbound_dissolution }
import std.types { List }
import std.markdown { MarkdownBlock, CodeBlock, CodeText, TableBlock, AlignNone }
import gunbc.plan { Plan, PlanRetiresWhen, PlanIsAuthorityOnly }
import gunbc.plans.md_helpers { h2, h3, p, li, ul, ol, cell, row }
import gunbc.design_ruling { project_documentation_projections_are_not_checkout_artifacts }

fn logical_work_realization_body() -> List<MarkdownBlock> {
  [
    p(text: "Proposal for review. Give ordinary callers a small logical interface for reads, writes and computations, with deployment-scoped SLO and arbitration defaults. This plan specifies the first consumer and the conditions for implementation; it does not implement implicit operand completion, change runtime policy, or authorize a deployment."),
    h2(text: "1. The consumer problem and intended interface"),
    p(text: "A caller should express the work and its irreducible inputs. Storage delegates to the existing fabric storage interface: fabric owns backend selection, placement and the selected backend's prerequisites. Worktree claims consume that interface rather than introducing a file-versus-network chooser of their own. The broader direction includes compute placement and reuse. Correctness requirements constrain admissible realizations; cost and service-level objectives guide the choice within those constraints. The first implementation should establish the interface and move consumers onto it using simple configured inputs, without waiting for production metering."),
    CodeBlock { segments: [CodeText { text: "// Desired consumer surface; illustrative, not implemented inference.\nworktree_claim_record_before_add(claim: claim)" }] },
    p(text: "The example proposes a replacement of the existing worktree_claim_record_before_add(root: NonEmptyStr, claim: WorktreeClaim) signature: root becomes a supplied realization dependency. It is not a second operation with the same name. Cut over the production consumer gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_belt_actuate and test.claim.roadmap.attempt_worktree_claim_wet_witness, along with the settlement entry points in the inventory."),
    p(text: "The operation and existing logical identity determine the requested resource; repeated use addresses the same authority under its existing semantics. The logical effects remain represented: pure computations, observed reads, durable mutations and fresh effects retain their own identity, freshness, ordering and retry contracts. The common completion path does not make a mutation memoizable."),
    h2(text: "2. One small policy surface"),
    p(text: "Ordinary calls inherit a scoped service/deployment profile. The optional surface has two concepts: SLO requirements and arbitration policy. A profile is a reference to their existing authorities, not a copy of owner, path, credentials, provider facts or per-operation knobs. Each inherited requirement must resolve to its owning declaration, cited by module and symbol; delivery 1 names those declarations. A required value with no such authority remains unresolved. An explicit declaration that the root adds no performance target is distinct from failing to find a required target. An explicit departure is stated at the scope that owns the requirement and cannot weaken the operation's mandatory contract."),
    CodeBlock { segments: [CodeText { text: "// Conceptual fabric-owned policy; not new .dag syntax or a new policy algebra.\nrealization_profile \{\n  slo: inherit_service_requirements,\n  arbitration: configured_file_and_r2_example,\n\}\n\n// Explicit example inputs for one fixed object put/readback workload:\n// backend       cost (micro-USD/operation)   latency (ms/operation)\n// local files   0                            0\n// R2            1                            1\n// These are supplied example predictions, not provider prices or measurements." }] },
    p(text: "The example deliberately supplies local cost/latency as 0/0 and R2 as positive values so local wins when both are admissible. Zero is an explicit example assumption, never a substitution for an unknown reading. The values carry their example/predicted standing into the SelectionReceipt evidence snapshot. Reuse std.realization_schedule::CostAxisPredicted and CostTimePredicted where those carriers fit, and extdeps.external_authority::CitedFigureStanding for an external figure's grounding; do not mint a measured receipt for supplied numbers. Replacing them with calibrated or metered inputs is a different decision through the same interface. An example prediction cannot establish a declared physical SLO floor."),
    p(text: "SLO means a named requirement with a subject, operation/workload, metric and units, bound, observation scope/window, evidence rule and consequence. A latency percentile without a population/window is incomplete. Existing requirements are inherited; this proposal invents no universal millisecond, availability or currency target. Cost objectives include the modeled costs of realizing and operating the choice, including setup, transfer and migration where applicable; an unknown cost is never zero."),
    h2(text: "3. Initial defaults and their limits"),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "Contract: inherit the operation's existing consistency, durability, retention, sharing, access and effect requirements. Performance preferences do not weaken them. Worktree claims additionally require enumeration for recovery and continuity of their authority."),
      li(text: "SLO: inherit established service/deployment requirements. If no additional performance target is declared, make no additional performance promise. A required but unknown bound or observation remains unresolved; it is not the same as no extra bound."),
      li(text: "Arbitration: fabric storage owns the local-file and R2 candidates and their configured example readings. Use those inputs immediately to exercise selection and adopt the interface. For already allocated mutable state, preserve its existing authority; an isolated fresh resource can exercise a different admitted backend without silently relocating live state."),
      li(text: "Selection: fabric consumes std.decision::select_realization and its SelectionReceipt, with std.pareto and the existing ValuedObjective machinery. UniqueSurvivorRequired handles a unique survivor; PreferSurvivor only selects a feasible survivor. No feature-specific scoring or list-order preference."),
      li(text: "Evidence: supplied example predictions can drive the pilot's choice under its declared policy. Required SLO floors still need their own admissible evidence and consequence; missing such evidence returns SelectionNeedsEvidence. Two surviving alternatives without an applicable policy return SelectionNeedsPolicy. Production metering is a later refinement, not an interface-adoption prerequisite."),
      li(text: "Prerequisites: use the selected realization's existing ensure, observation and authorization routes under the responsible root's authority. Correct existing state is Noop. Missing authority is never manufactured by the constructor."),
      li(text: "Continuity: keep a mutable resource's identity across calls and restarts. An unavailable authoritative store refuses; it does not become an empty local store. Moving existing state is a separately admitted transition whose correctness and cost are part of the decision."),
    ]),
    p(text: "The two-backend example must execute both choices. In the first isolated context, both are admissible and local wins on the supplied inputs. In the second, a declared sharing/reachability requirement excludes the host-local candidate before ranking, so R2 wins if it meets that requirement. Name the actual candidate scope: fabric's served file backend can also be shared, so being file-backed alone is not evidence of host-local reach. Keep the logical caller unchanged. Changing the supplied readings in a separate selection control should also change a feasible winner; neither exercise claims measured economics or permits migration of existing state."),
    h2(text: "4. Existing authorities and the missing connections"),
    p(text: "This program's subject is the logical consumer's common authoring surface across reads, writes and computations. Environmental readiness is one completion route it consumes; selection and immutable-result reuse retain their own authorities. That broader consumer scope is why its single governance row is at the compiler architecture, rather than assigning the whole program to the environmental specialization."),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "std.fabric_storage is the storage interface: FabricObject, FabricHeadExpectation, FabricPut, FabricHeadRead, FabricHeadAdvance and FabricClosureRead already compose immutable objects and conditional named heads. gunbc.fabric.fabric_storage_client exposes fabric_storage_put, fabric_storage_head, fabric_storage_advance and fabric_storage_closure over FabricStorageBinding. Use these authorities rather than adding a logical-storage interface beside them."),
      li(text: "gunbc.fabric.fabric_storage_file_store implements files; gunbc.fabric.fabric_object_r2 provides put_fabric_object_r2 and get_fabric_object_r2; gunbc.fabric.fabric_storage_r2_head provides r2_head_read and r2_head_advance. R2 is not yet an arm of FabricStorageBinding. The client also lacks object-get, although std.fabric_storage::FabricObjectGet and fabric_storage_file_store::fabric_storage_file_get already exist: delivery 1 carries those existing operations/results through the shared binding for independent readback. Object put/readback need not publish a head merely to read an object. Composing the remaining operations is fabric work, including object-before-head publication, closure reads, CAS admission and uncertain-write outcomes. Reuse the backend implementations; production cost instruments are not a prerequisite."),
      li(text: "gunbc.fabric.fabric_storage_placement and fabric_storage_binding own current placement/access routing. The placed shared store's clients reach its admitted door/socket or HTTPS route. Separately admitted host-local stores also exist: gunbc.compute.host_capacity::compute_capacity_store constructs FabricStorageLocalFiles for its ledger. Preserve each store's declared scope; the local binding is not permission to bypass the shared store's admission because configured cost is zero."),
      li(text: "std.decision::select_realization and std.pareto own candidate constraints, evidence and selection. SelectionReceipt identifies the scoped choice. The profile above projects into those models rather than introducing another decision algebra."),
      li(text: "gunbc.ensure and gunbc.owned_directory::owned_directory_ensure already support real consumers and observe/decide/apply/readback behavior. std.realization_reconcile::ConvergedEffect classifies supplied reports; by itself it does not establish that the selected effect actually ran or produced the observation."),
      li(text: "std.materialization_ladder and std.materialization_provider own reuse of admitted immutable results. The ladder explicitly excludes mutable keyed state. Extending the common authoring experience must preserve that distinction."),
      li(text: "gunbc.plans.v2_compiler_architecture owns completion and residuals; gunbc.plans.ensure_closure_design owns the environmental specialization. Omitted-operand completion is a target, not a capability supplied by this proposal. Today's dashboard_instance_directories::dashboard_instance_directory_demands remains authored."),
      li(text: "gunbc.auth.authorization_pattern_selection::select_authorization_pattern selects an existing authorization mechanism; privileged_effect_census describes coverage. A constructor cannot confer an authority the deployment does not possess."),
    ]),
    p(text: "The selection-to-effect connection remains a frontier at the shared protocol layer. std.goal_assessment explicitly reserves admission, actuation and post-actuation re-observation for its first real consumer, gunbc.fleet.fleet_converge_plan with generation, held lease, observed baseline and compare-and-set; the trigger is that spine binding the effectful half. gunbc.plans.convergence_coverage_program also declines to mint it. This pilot does not create or wait for a competing shared cycle. It closes each selected realization through existing gunbc.ensure and the domain's executed observation route, keeping the selected binding as the actual operand to put/get and retaining route-discriminating evidence. A supplied-report classifier alone cannot establish execution. Changes to the subject, candidate field, constraints, policy or evidence invalidate the old selection."),
    p(text: "The second join is consumer demand to prerequisites. For the bounded pilot, model the necessary facts at the owning interface before changing callers and derive setup/use from the same values. A second handwritten store registry is not completion. General inference belongs to the existing compiler and demand-engine plans; wiring one known route does not establish universal closure."),
    p(text: "The third join is a useful diagnostic. Existing domains have typed refusal outcomes; this proposal does not declare that a generic residual carrier already exists. At the pilot boundary, WorktreeClaimNotRecorded currently carries detail: String, flattening distinct causes such as lost race and readback mismatch. The domain migration identifies the existing lower-level reasons and their owners so the outcome can preserve them instead of inventing a parallel taxonomy. A missing derivation carries the dependency path and the authority that can answer it. A closed operation's I/O refusal or contention remains its runtime outcome."),
    h2(text: "5. First worked behavior: worktree claims"),
    p(text: "A worktree is a Git checkout. The worktree-claims directory stores ownership records; it is not the checkout itself. gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_attempt_worktree_claim::worktree_claim_record_before_add writes a create-only claim and verifies it before git worktree add. Its settlement path uses cas_slot_keys to enumerate records. The motivating classes are gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_store_root_nothing_creates and gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.an_attempt_worktree_has_no_owner_until_the_attempt_state_exists."),
    p(text: "The existing root declaration, roadmap_attempt_worktree_claim_root::worktree_claim_slots_directory, already derives path and owner from HostDashboardInstance and declares DirectoryOwnerOnly. Deployment separately enrolls it; runtime independently passes the root. The migration moves storage responsibility into fabric's existing contract and setup route, preserving the domain's behavior while removing consumer-owned directory enrollment and raw-root plumbing."),
    p(text: "The record operation already calls worktree_claim_open, reads through worktree_claim_read, and compares claim identity and worktree path. Preserve that executed readback as the baseline; the missing selection-to-effect connection is above it. Keep the existing attempt lifecycle, publication, retention and recovery semantics. Trace worktree_claim_open through gunbc.compute.attempt_lifecycle::attempt_open_payload and its file_compare_and_set route before selecting a replacement; do not substitute the windowed/head-only API merely because it also offers conditional update. The fabric candidate must additionally establish enumeration, retention, consistency scope and authority continuity before it can serve this whole behavior."),
    p(text: "The R2 head's conditional publication already has a declaration: fabric_storage_r2_head::r2_head_advance_plan uses PutIfAbsent or PutIfMatch, and r2_head_fabric_advance requires R2HeadCasAdmitted. Preserve that admission; low example cost cannot supply it. FabricClosureRead follows links from a known head and is not enumeration of all claim keys. Recovery therefore needs a fabric-owned representation/operation that preserves today's cas_slot_keys behavior. That is a claim-migration obligation, separate from exercising object storage selection on both existing backends."),
    CodeBlock { segments: [CodeText { text: "logical claim operation\n  -> existing domain contract\n  -> std.fabric_storage operations\n  -> fabric-owned file/R2 selection and SelectionReceipt\n  -> selected backend's access, setup, admission and readback\n  -> domain result through the selected binding\n\nExample unresolved path:\nrecord claim -> fabric storage -> selected backend -> consumer access\nOwner to answer: deployment/access authority" }] },
    h2(text: "6. Three bounded deliveries"),
    ol(items: [
      li(text: "Fabric interface and two-backend example. Use gunbc.instruments.source_snapshot_handoff::source_snapshot_handoff and gunbc.fabric.fabric_source_snapshot::\{capture_source_snapshot, materialize_source_snapshot\} as the first complete consumer. Replace the concrete file-root dependency with the shared fabric binding; preserve composition, inclusions, manifest and local provider-workspace semantics. Carry the existing object put/get operations and required result distinctions through file and R2 realizations. The existing no-argument instrument root supplies the fabric-owned example policy once. Execute its synthetic snapshot capture/materialization through both selected backends and retain the actual child-process control. This establishes executed interface adoption, not a claim of production rollout. No heads, claim enumeration or production metering are prerequisites for this slice."),
      li(text: "One complete domain consumer. Enumerate claim record, read, conditional-update and settlement callers; map their requirements to fabric's existing models and name any missing recovery operation. Land missing contracts before migrating. Connect selection, prerequisites, actual admission, execution and readback across recording and settlement plus both deployment routes. Preserve existing publication, retention and recovery. Keep necessary platform binding at the fabric/deployment root, consumed by both setup and use; delete independent consumer setup enrollment."),
      li(text: "Adoption and refinement. Prove the migrated logical caller unchanged in a second isolated deployment, with unsupported domain operations excluded before backend ranking. Exercise the shared interface on both backends for their admitted operations. Add calibrated or metered inputs later through the same fabric policy and receipt, without changing consumers. The pilot does not require live migration, every provider, general prerequisite inference or completion of the whole compiler."),
    ]),
    p(text: "Use the remaining explicit wiring from these deliveries to identify the next small completion obligation in the existing compiler program. Credential-acquisition and session-placement stores are subsequent comparison cases, not prerequisites for finishing the first example. Approval consolidation is a separate follow-up: sensitivity in context and one route for the formal approvals that remain."),
    h2(text: "7. Evidence and conformance review"),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "Start the real-path witness with only the parent directory. Derive/provision the child under the admitted authority and perform the actual record/read/enumeration route as the consumer principal. Repeat directory/setup reconciliation to establish Noop; a duplicate claim write must retain its existing lost-race/refusal behavior. Preserve a real producer-path witness alongside inexpensive supplied-boundary tests."),
      li(text: "Delete prerequisite production and require the migrated operation to fail before a successful claim write or checkout launch. Wrong instance, foreign ownership, inaccessible state and failed readback must not produce a usable store. State whether each protection is model construction, compile-time admission or runtime refusal."),
      li(text: "The explicit local 0/0 and R2 positive example selects local when both are admissible; a second context that excludes local selects R2 and performs its real put/readback. A supplied-input control changes the feasible winner when readings change. The receipts retain example standing. A required performance floor without admissible evidence returns SelectionNeedsEvidence; synthetic predictions do not satisfy it. An absent optional SLO creates no promise."),
      li(text: "Changing a selection input invalidates its receipt. A post-actuation response cannot retroactively prove that admission happened before the effect. Model ordering at the effectful construction boundary and observe uncertain completion before retry according to the existing recovery law."),
      li(text: "An unavailable authoritative store must not be interpreted as absence or trigger a fresh fallback store. Equivalent behavior and refusal semantics, not merely the same method signatures, establish provider compatibility."),
      li(text: "Review asks what the author still supplies, why the shared model cannot derive it, and what integration points disappeared. Recognizing a competing representation remains a judgment. Do not add a universal conformance checker or a test that only asserts the new declaration exists."),
    ]),
    h2(text: "8. Open implementation questions"),
    ol(items: [
      li(text: "Where should fabric's existing placement/binding policy carry the initial configured readings and inherited service requirements? Reuse existing decision, measure and evidence-standing carriers. The two policy concepts above do not justify a new generic profile or storage authority."),
      li(text: "The shared SelectionReceipt -> admission -> actuation -> independent observation protocol stays at std.goal_assessment's declared frontier until the fleet admission spine binds it. The pilot uses existing ensure and executed readback, with no new shared cycle. The deployment-gate stage-2 proposal [gunbc#14757](https://github.com/gunb-ai/gunbc/pull/14757) is a domain example of confined phase inputs and request-bound responses, not the shared home. Coordinate concrete prerequisite typing and selection-to-use evidence with the convergence owner."),
      li(text: "What fabric-owned enumeration or index operation preserves worktree recovery, and how do R2 object/head/closure operations compose behind FabricStorageBinding? Resolve those contracts in their current homes. Keep the object put/readback example moving while the full domain migration is specified."),
      li(text: "Which remaining explicit dependency can the current compiler derive next without a new syntax or wrapper around an unresolved model deficit? The pilot supplies the concrete input to that decision."),
    ]),
    h2(text: "9. Staffing, migration decisions and completion"),
    p(text: "This is a design and staffing plan; the packages below are proposed responsibility boundaries, not dispatched assignments or implemented capabilities. Use one fabric integration owner and one complete claim-migration owner, with directory, R2 and deployment reviewers. Split parallel work at stable domain contracts; do not hand independent layers to owners who each invent their own binding, setup list or result projection."),
    h3(text: "The smallest consumer and its honest authoring boundary"),
    CodeBlock { segments: [CodeText { text: "// Existing external instrument entry remains:\nsource_snapshot_handoff()\n\n// Proposed replacements of existing internal signatures:\ncapture_source_snapshot(\n  store: FabricStorageBinding,\n  composition: SourceComposition,\n  inclusions: List<SnapshotInclusion>,\n) -> SnapshotCapture\n\nmaterialize_source_snapshot(\n  store: FabricStorageBinding,\n  manifest: FabricObjectRef,\n  workspace: ProviderWorkspace,\n  expected: SourceComposition,\n) -> SnapshotMaterialization" }] },
    p(text: "The root resolves the fabric-owned deployment policy and supplies one selected binding to both operations. Consumers describe composition, inclusions and the manifest; they do not choose buckets, physical roots or credentials. This explicit internal dependency is implementable with the existing language. The illustrative claim-only call in section 1 remains the compiler-completion target, not an assertion that omitted operands already elaborate. Initial 0/0 versus 1/1 inputs describe one fixed object put/readback pair; the snapshot is the integration workload, and those figures do not claim total snapshot latency or cost."),
    p(text: "The pilot preserves existing content checks and exact-preimage readback without claiming cryptographic object identity; gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.fabric_object_identity_is_a_structural_locator remains the owning frontier."),
    h3(text: "Prerequisites compose through existing goal assessment"),
    p(text: "For the selected realization only, type a product goal and component evidence at the fabric/domain boundary. Reuse gunbc.ensure::EnsurePolicy, EnsureObservation and ensure_observation_as_attempt with std.goal_assessment::\{inspect_goal, assess_by_deviations_and_unknowns, GoalAssessment\}. The pilot domain assessor constructs GoalSatisfied only after observing every required component; the generic carrier does not derive that population or establish that observation executed. Keep the observer goal-blind and preserve GoalAssessmentRefused for malformed or mismatched subjects. GoalDiverged and GoalIndeterminate retain typed deviations/unknowns, and an observation refusal stays outside the assessment. Use EnsureObserveOnly for prerequisite assessment. Where the responsible root already has applicable authority, its existing ensure route may apply and independently read back before assessment. Ordinary put/get consumers do not thereby acquire new bootstrap authority. Selecting local files does not require provisioning R2."),
    p(text: "R2's gunbc.cloudflare.r2_bucket_ensure::\{ensure_r2_purpose_bucket, ensure_r2_purpose, apply_r2_bucket_create\} already executes bucket GET/readback, but R2PurposeEnsureOutcome \{ line, held \} is not reusable observation evidence, and its effectful entry points lack an observe-only policy operand. Map real reads through EnsureObservation at that owning boundary; unavailable observation stays unknown/refused. gunbc.fabric.fabric_blob_r2::FabricBlobTargetReady resolves configuration and never serves as GoalSatisfied evidence. Preserve directional credentials and staging custody through the existing routes. Use the existing FabricWorkspace purpose for the synthetic workspace-object pilot; its declared retention is not proof of observed lifecycle configuration: ensure_r2_purpose currently skips lifecycle observation when the desired rule list is empty. Close that distinction before admitting a durable domain that relies on absence of deletion rules."),
    p(text: "Keep the pilot goal as corpus-declared data. std.goal_assessment intentionally carries no goal revision today; adding a runtime-changing profile without binding its revision would admit stale readiness. The goal-revision and shared effectful-protocol triggers belong to the existing fleet plan basis, not a new profile invented by this pilot."),
    TableBlock {
      header: row(cells: [cell(text: "Work package"), cell(text: "Proposed owner and sequencing"), cell(text: "Required handback")]),
      alignments: [AlignNone, AlignNone, AlignNone],
      rows: [
        row(cells: [cell(text: "R1. File readiness repair"), cell(text: "Directory/fabric owner; independently staffable now. Coordinate the existing host-capacity and instrument callers."), cell(text: "Replace exit-status-only Ready with the existing owned-directory observe/decide/apply/readback route. Preserve parent authority and host-local ledger scope; prove inaccessible/foreign/mismatched directories cannot qualify use. This repairs the identified current defect.")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "R2. R2 prerequisite evidence"), cell(text: "R2 owner paired with the fabric integrator; can proceed beside R1 using the existing goal/ensure models."), cell(text: "Expose actual bucket, allocation and directional credential observations as typed evidence under observe-only versus authorized apply. Reuse allocation, secret and transfer routes. Ordinary data consumers do not acquire bucket-admin authority. Distinguish configured target resolution, observed readiness, unknowns and observation refusal.")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "F. Shared fabric contract and routes"), cell(text: "One fabric integrator owns the model, bindings, codecs and all direct result consumers together; takes R1/R2 evidence shapes before execution is connected."), cell(text: "Model uncertain completion/custody and operation capability at existing authorities before changing adapters. Add R2 object put/get and served get-by-ref; preserve protected state admission. Disposition every closed binding/result match in the compatibility inventory in the same delivery. Unsupported heads/closure remain excluded before selection, never fabricated success.")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "S. Source-snapshot vertical slice"), cell(text: "Same fabric integrator or a consumer owner after F, R1 and R2 agree; owns capture through final child-process outcome."), cell(text: "Keep source_snapshot_handoff() unchanged externally. Capture child objects before parent/manifest, materialize through the selected binding, then execute the existing child control. Both backends run with supplied-standing receipts; missing prerequisites, denied access, failed readback, unresolved puts and cleanup residue cannot become complete success. Keep destructive provider fixtures isolated.")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "C1. Claim contract and state transition"), cell(text: "One claim/lifecycle owner; design can run beside S. Review with fabric and deployment owners before the cut."), cell(text: "Name the logical namespace, scoped enumeration, retained-history obligation and existing-state transition. Reuse lifecycle/codec/admit_callers authority. Account for the shared lifecycle's other consumers without silently moving their state. No claim backend is eligible until the whole record/read/update/enumerate contract is established.")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "C2. Complete claim cutover"), cell(text: "The C1 owner carries recording, recovery, both setup routes and evidence through one complete consumer cut; depends on F and the admitted C1 contracts."), cell(text: "Cut over the two production entrances and disposition all 13 direct call sites. Internal helpers may disappear when the new root covers their surviving obligations. Update sealed admission references and derived grants, retire independent claim-directory enrollment/root plumbing, and preserve checkout/unit/capture semantics. Rehearse state continuity and restart/recovery before any deployment. The old consumer route ends without a fallback.")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "Later adoption cohorts"), cell(text: "Staff individually from the closed direct-consumer inventory after their exact domain obligations are dispositioned."), cell(text: "Credentials, placement, journals, security state and other stores are separate consumer contracts. Shared-result compatibility work is immediate when that result changes; backend migration is separately scoped. Approval policy/route consolidation returns as the next design discussion, not as a hidden dependency of storage.")]),
      ],
    },
    h3(text: "Existing state and the production cut"),
    p(text: "A fresh isolated snapshot can select either backend without a data migration. Existing claim stores cannot. Before staffing a production cut, the C1 handback names every admitted source namespace and consumer, how writers and recovery are quiesced or otherwise fenced, how existing records and required generations are represented and independently reconciled at the destination, and the single authority switch. Failed preparation keeps the original authority; after new writes begin, switching back to an old snapshot is not a rollback. Any reverse transition requires its own continuity proof. These are design obligations, not authorization to stop a service, copy private state or change a live binding."),
    p(text: "Recovery today enumerates keys and reads each current claim; that does not by itself prove a requirement to traverse every historical generation. The current unwindowed store retains its generation line, while fabric CAS uses generation-bearing link-free objects and per-key heads. State explicitly which retention/audit/compatibility obligations survive and name their authority before choosing a representation; do not erase retained data as an incidental refactor or require a new history API merely by assuming recovery uses one. Fabric CAS's cas-slot- prefix alone also does not carry the old host/instance/store namespace."),
    h3(text: "When the design can be handed to implementers"),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "Each chosen workflow has a named entry, deployment/subject scope, principal/access route, ordinary execution and recovery/retirement path. The checked-in built-in roster and externally supplied instances remain distinct; Brian's workflow names close the operational scope that source searches cannot establish."),
      li(text: "At each replaced boundary, every observed consumer and witness has a disposition: retain under a named surviving contract, replace with its owning authority, keep as evidence, or retire with a reason. Use the existing gunbc.replacement_cut vocabulary and replacement-migration doctrine when the implementation cut is modeled. Required emitted CI closures alone are not the census."),
      li(text: "The staffing package names the exact unresolved model decision, its owning module, dependencies and discriminating evidence. A bounded modeling package may be staffed before its implementation contract is settled; it must not be handed off as an implementation-ready interface."),
      li(text: "Completion of an implementation cut requires zero undispositioned consumers and zero uncovered surviving consumers, the exact new population executing through its one authority, no old-route fallback or migration flags, reconciled subject identities, and retained/retired evidence accounted for. These are the existing doctrine's criteria, not a percentage confidence target."),
      li(text: "One real route per admitted backend must survive alongside cheaper supplied-boundary controls. Removing readiness production, using the wrong scope/principal, injecting an unresolved publication or preventing independent readback must stop complete success. Claim duplicates, lost close races, unreadable enumeration and crash gaps retain their distinct outcomes."),
    ]),
    h2(text: "Appendix: migration sites and expected behavior"),
    p(text: "Source inventory updated on 2026-10-22 at proposal 7be4375e5a19. The core fabric, claim, lifecycle, ensure and goal-assessment authorities were also checked against main cac57613cc92 and were unchanged; the full census is pinned to the proposal snapshot, not a claim about every later main revision. These are implementation sites and expected changes, not migrations executed by this design PR. Sections A-D describe behavior and delivery scope; section E closes specific tracked-source operation populations. Those bounded censuses do not claim all filesystem I/O, external repositories or deployed reachability."),
    p(text: "The current claim boundary has two production entry call sites in roadmap_belt_actuate, seven claim-domain functions taking root/claims_root, one independently authored directory enrollment and two provisioning paths. The counts describe the named sites below, not a gate or an implementation budget. Additional shared fabric result/identity users need review if their closed contracts change."),
    h3(text: "A. Shared fabric work required by the first pilot"),
    TableBlock {
      header: row(cells: [cell(text: "Sites"), cell(text: "Migration or reuse"), cell(text: "Expected behavior and invariants")]),
      alignments: [AlignNone, AlignNone, AlignNone],
      rows: [
        row(cells: [cell(text: "std.fabric_storage::FabricPut; gunbc.fabric.fabric_storage_client::FabricStorageBinding, fabric_storage_put, fabric_storage_head, fabric_storage_advance, fabric_storage_closure"), cell(text: "Add the R2 realization and carry the existing object-get contract through the client. Reuse FabricObjectGet and the file/R2 provider operations. Model shared uncertain-publication handling before adapting callers."), cell(text: "R2 may answer that a put's completion is unknown; today's FabricPut only has stored/refused. Preserve that distinction and required readback, plus credential/staging custody. Never convert uncertainty into absence, success or a definite failure.")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "gunbc.fabric.fabric_storage_file_store::fabric_storage_file_get, fabric_storage_file_put; gunbc.fabric.fabric_object_r2::put_fabric_object_r2, get_fabric_object_r2"), cell(text: "Reuse these implementations behind fabric's common binding. The first example puts and reads the object without publishing a head."), cell(text: "Both choices execute the same logical workload. Existing content checks, create-only/idempotent publication semantics and R2 cleanup remain. The example's 0/0 inputs do not promise physically free or instantaneous I/O.")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "gunbc.fabric.fabric_blob_r2::resolve_fabric_blob_target, resolve_fabric_blob_target_under; gunbc.cloudflare.r2_origin::bucket_purpose_origin_standing; gunbc.cloudflare.r2_staged_transfer::r2_put_staged_file, r2_fetch_into_staging, r2_release_staging"), cell(text: "Reuse existing account/bucket/purpose and directional credential resolution, transfer and staging cleanup under the selected R2 binding."), cell(text: "Preserve specific missing-allocation and credential refusals plus credential/staging custody. The feature consumer does not acquire a second credential or setup route.")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "gunbc.fabric.fabric_source_snapshot::snapshot_store_inclusion, capture_source_snapshot, snapshot_materialize_entry_links, snapshot_materialize_step, materialize_source_snapshot; workspace_checkpoint_instrument::workspace_instrument_commit_admitted, workspace_stored_entry_read"), cell(text: "These are existing object-consumer adoption sites: source snapshots use the concrete file object store, while workspace checkpoints directly use R2. Select a bounded object-only consumer for the initial shared-interface demonstration; retain intentional provider-specific fixtures."), cell(text: "Preserve manifest child-before-parent publication and materialization checks. The checkpoint commit also advances an R2 head: its object half cannot independently switch backend while that head stays elsewhere. It is a later composed migration, not an object-only cutover.")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "gunbc.fabric.fabric_storage_protocol::fabric_storage_respond; fabric_storage_wire::fabric_storage_wire_put, fabric_storage_unwire_put; fabric_storage_state_auth::fabric_state_operation"), cell(text: "Add served object-get and its request/result codec; extend the closed operation admission where get traverses the door. Update put codecs if its shared result grows."), cell(text: "Preserve the protected /state namespace and writer/reader admission. Get-by-ref must not expose private objects through a public route. Unknown operations and malformed replies still refuse.")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "gunbc.fabric.fabric_storage_state_auth_io::fabric_state_signed_request, fabric_state_verified_request; fabric_storage_state_serve::fabric_storage_state_serve_over; fabric_storage_serve::fabric_served_storage_respond, fabric_storage_protected_door_over, fabric_storage_serve_handle"), cell(text: "Check the full served-get path against the existing authentication and routing boundaries; reuse those mechanisms instead of creating a second approval/access route."), cell(text: "The new operation must be reachable through the same admitted route and principal. A zero local selection input does not authorize bypassing the door or a protected state signature.")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "gunbc.fabric.fabric_storage_placement::fabric_storage_directory_demands, fabric_storage_placed_file_root; fabric_storage_binding::fabric_storage_binding_for, fabric_state_storage_binding; fabric_storage_client::fabric_storage_presented_identity; fabric_writer_identity_observe::binding_words"), cell(text: "House selection and supplied readings at fabric's existing placement/binding boundary. Connect selected readiness and update exhaustive binding/identity readers for R2."), cell(text: "Preserve the placed shared store's serving admission; separately admitted host-local stores retain their declared scope. R2 has its own credential/identity requirements; do not manufacture a tailnet identity for it. Preserve existing state authority when choosing an operation's binding.")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "gunbc.fabric.fabric_storage_file_store::fabric_storage_file_root_ensure; gunbc.owned_directory::owned_directory_ensure"), cell(text: "The file-root helper currently runs Mkdir.Parents for objects/heads and checks command success. Connect the selected provider to the existing owned-directory observation/apply/readback route."), cell(text: "FabricStorageRootReady from that helper is not proof of correct owner/mode or independent readback. The completed interface must establish readiness under the admitted principal; unqualified existing directories may now refuse.")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "gunbc.fabric.fabric_storage_r2_head::r2_head_advance_plan, r2_head_advance, r2_head_fabric_advance; std.fabric_storage::FabricHeadAdvance, FabricClosureRead"), cell(text: "For head-using consumers, compose the existing R2 object and head operations, publication ordering and closure walk. Keep this separate from the first object-only example."), cell(text: "PutIfAbsent/PutIfMatch and R2HeadCasAdmitted remain prerequisites. Publish objects before heads, retain lost-race and uncertain-completion behavior, and preserve history. A closure walk is not enumeration of all claims.")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "gunbc.fabric.fabric_event_log::event_log_append_with, event_log_append; durable_cas_fabric_storage::fabric_storage_compare_and_set, fabric_storage_observe_cas_slot"), cell(text: "These already consume fabric. Adapt their result handling if the common put/advance outcomes change; they do not need another storage migration."), cell(text: "Keep append/CAS conflict semantics and durable history. Handle any newly expressible uncertain result through observation/recovery. Enumerate their callers before changing a public outcome, rather than flattening it to retain the old signature. This attempt did not advance the head when its advance step never ran, while object publication/custody may remain unresolved. Another writer may still have advanced the head; do not label every enclosing result unknown mechanically.")]),
      ],
    },
    p(text: "Current convergence defect, separate from interface adoption: gunbc.fabric.fabric_storage_file_store::fabric_storage_file_root_ensure constructs FabricStorageRootReady solely from successful Mkdir.Parents results, without independent directory observation. This is an instance of the existing gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.control_plane_acknowledgement_minted_as_effect::control_plane_acknowledgement_minted_as_effect class at the helper's readiness boundary; DESIGN section 3d forbids an actuation return from minting convergence. In gunbc.compute.host_capacity, compute_capacity_store_ensure feeds compute_reserve_against, which accepts Ready before compute_seat. Deployment does converge the parent compute_root_directory, but no corresponding owner/mode/readback covers the derived capacity, objects and heads directories before Ready is consumed. Later ledger I/O can refuse storage failures without proving directory identity/access. gunbc.instruments.source_snapshot_handoff::prepare_snapshot_workspace and fabric_event_log_probe::fabric_event_log_probe also consume the result. This is a source-established evidence gap, not a recorded live permissions incident or a claim that the ledger already records this specimen. Correct this readiness boundary through the existing owned-directory and effectful observation route independently of R2, cost selection or general compiler completion."),
    h3(text: "B. Worktree-claim migration and its existing callers"),
    TableBlock {
      header: row(cells: [cell(text: "Sites"), cell(text: "Migration or reuse"), cell(text: "Expected behavior and invariants")]),
      alignments: [AlignNone, AlignNone, AlignNone],
      rows: [
        row(cells: [cell(text: "gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_belt_actuate::belt_worktree_claim_before_add, belt_spawn_admitted"), cell(text: "Remove claim-root derivation from the caller and supply the scoped fabric dependency through the existing application root."), cell(text: "Preserve the clock/deadline checks and record/readback-before-git-worktree-add ordering. Readiness, selection or storage failure still prevents checkout launch. The Git checkout itself remains on its execution host.")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_belt_actuate::belt_worktree_claim_ensure, belt_session_settlement_pass, belt_tick_for_instance"), cell(text: "Recovery consumes the same logical storage binding as recording. Remove the second raw-root argument at the recovery entrance."), cell(text: "Preserve session settlement and activation reconciliation before claim cleanup, and settlement before new acquisition. Red claim outcomes still refuse the settlement pass.")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_attempt_worktree_claim::worktree_claim_read, worktree_claim_open, worktree_claim_close, worktree_claim_record_before_add, worktree_claim_close_recorded, worktree_claim_ensure_one, worktree_claim_ensure_pass_at"), cell(text: "Disposition all seven raw-root functions through the complete consumer replacement. Surviving public operations use the domain's supplied fabric dependency; internal helpers may retire when their surviving obligations are covered at the new root. Do not preserve obsolete helpers merely to translate their signatures."), cell(text: "Preserve absent/held/unreadable distinctions, duplicate-claim refusal, expected-generation updates, identity/path readback and cleanup order. Keep live, dirty, unpushed, foreign or uncertain trees; remove only an admitted tree, observe absence, then close its claim.")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "gunbc.compute.attempt_lifecycle::attempt_open_payload, attempt_terminate_payload, attempt_advance_payload, attempt_commit_bytes"), cell(text: "Consume the needed storage realization at the existing lifecycle authority, retaining its transition/codec checks. Do not reimplement the lifecycle in claims."), cell(text: "Preserve reference/deadline/generation checks, terminal reasons and retained history. Other lifecycle consumers remain a compatibility obligation; moving this shared boundary does not authorize migrating all their data or replacing unwindowed CAS with head-only retention.")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_attempt_worktree_claim::worktree_claim_ensure_pass_at; gunbc.durable_cas_file_store::cas_slot_keys"), cell(text: "Replace physical slot enumeration with a fabric-owned operation or index covering the same logical claim population."), cell(text: "Recover every claim, including one left before checkout creation. Enumeration refusal fails the pass; an inaccessible store is not empty. Do not substitute a scan of worktree directories or a closure from one already-known head.")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_attempt_worktree_claim_root::worktree_claim_slots_root, worktree_claim_slots_root_of, worktree_claim_slots_directory; roadmap_dashboard_instance::DispatchStateScope, dashboard_instance_dispatch_attempt_state_root"), cell(text: "Retire feature-owned physical root construction after fabric owns readiness; carry the old root's logical namespace into the fabric binding."), cell(text: "Preserve DispatchStateInstanceOwned versus DispatchStateHostShared. A naive instance_id prefix changes the intended sharing/exclusion boundary. Current records need an explicit continuity/cutover disposition; selecting a fresh empty store is not migration.")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "gunbc.roadmap.dashboard_instance_directories::dashboard_instance_directory_demands; roadmap_dashboard_instance_apply::dashboard_apply_owned_directories, dashboard_apply_directories_then_plan, dashboard_observe_owned_directories, dashboard_instance_ensure_dispatch_roots"), cell(text: "Remove the independent worktree_claim_slots_directory enrollment once the dashboard provisioning/readback route consumes selected fabric requirements."), cell(text: "The feature author no longer adds a second setup row. Preserve existing apply authority, observation-only refusals, failure ordering and independent readiness readback. Unrelated directory demands remain their own consumers.")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "gunbc.live_deploy.spec::deployment_spec_for, deployment_directory_demands; emit::owned_directory_apply_steps, owned_directory_fragments; member_observe::deployment_member_roster, observe_owned_directory, deployment_identity_readback; gunbc.runner.runner_host_grants::dashboard_directory_observation_operations_of"), cell(text: "Make the live-deployment spec, emitted apply, readback roster and derived observation grants consume the same selected fabric requirements as dashboard provisioning."), cell(text: "Keep current principal/access restrictions and post-apply readback. Moving the claim directory out of the feature list must not leave stale grants, omit the fabric prerequisite, or add a second independently maintained demand list.")]),
      ],
    },
    h3(text: "B1. Closed claim boundary and workflow roots"),
    p(text: "At 7be4375e5a19, the seven functions have 13 direct static calls: eight internal, two external production and three external test calls. The first column below is in gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_attempt_worktree_claim; unqualified internal callers are in that module. Test callers are in test.claim.roadmap. This is an exact source-call population for these symbols, not execution coverage. Internal helper retention is a disposition, not an obligation to translate every old helper into a new one."),
    TableBlock {
      header: row(cells: [cell(text: "Function"), cell(text: "Actual callers"), cell(text: "Disposition")]),
      alignments: [AlignNone, AlignNone, AlignNone],
      rows: [
        row(cells: [cell(text: "worktree_claim_read"), cell(text: "worktree_claim_record_before_add; worktree_claim_ensure_one; worktree_claim_ensure_pass_at"), cell(text: "Three internal calls; replace the concrete store dependency while retaining absent/held/unreadable semantics.")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "worktree_claim_open"), cell(text: "worktree_claim_record_before_add"), cell(text: "One internal call; retain the shared lifecycle and codec admission.")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "worktree_claim_close"), cell(text: "worktree_claim_close_recorded"), cell(text: "One internal call; retain expected-generation close.")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "worktree_claim_record_before_add"), cell(text: "Production: roadmap_belt_actuate::belt_worktree_claim_before_add. Test: attempt_worktree_claim_wet_witness::open_claim."), cell(text: "Two external entrances; cut over together.")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "worktree_claim_close_recorded"), cell(text: "Two arms of worktree_claim_ensure_one"), cell(text: "Both close-only and remove/readback/close paths must be covered.")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "worktree_claim_ensure_one"), cell(text: "worktree_claim_ensure_pass_at"), cell(text: "One internal call; preserve re-derived path and host-observation safeguards.")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "worktree_claim_ensure_pass_at"), cell(text: "Production: roadmap_belt_actuate::belt_worktree_claim_ensure. Tests: attempt_worktree_claim_wet_witness::\{pass, a_git_that_could_not_run_is_red_and_keeps_the_tree\}."), cell(text: "Three external entrances; retain complete scoped enumeration and refusal behavior.")]),
      ],
    },
    p(text: "Also preserve or deliberately replace the confined declaration references: worktree_claim_codec admits worktree_claim_open/worktree_claim_close; gunbc.compute.attempt_lifecycle::\{attempt_open_payload, attempt_terminate_payload\} admits those same domain producers. The wet witness imports worktree_claim_open without calling it; remove that unused import, do not count it as another entrance. worktree_claim_slots_root is used only by worktree_claim_slots_root_of; that helper feeds the declaration and two production entrances. There is one directory-list enrollment, consumed by two provisioning mechanisms."),
    CodeBlock { segments: [CodeText { text: "launch obligation -> belt_instance_obligation_run\n  -> belt_run_once_cli_in -> belt_run_once_in -> belt_tick_for_instance\n     -> belt_session_settlement_pass\n        -> session settlement -> activation reconciliation -> claim recovery\n     -> belt_tick_spawn_after_settlement\n        -> belt_actuate_spawn_with_origin -> belt_spawn_admitted\n           -> record claim + independent readback -> Git worktree add" }] },
    p(text: "The obligation route is gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_belt_tick_cli::belt_instance_obligation_run; the emitted service queues it through belt_launch_enqueue_cli. Runtime instance resolution uses GUNBC_BELT_SPAWN_WORKDIR and dashboard_instance_for_repo_root. Preserve this actual entry selection; the convenience belt_tick/belt_run_once projections are not evidence that another deployment ran."),
    p(text: "Provisioning entrypoints to keep on the same derived requirements: gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_dashboard_instance_apply::\{dashboard_instance_ensure_roots_cli, macbook_local_ensure_roots_cli, srv2_deploy_ensure_roots_cli, srv1_lab_dashboard_apply_wet, srv2_lab_dashboard_apply_wet\}; gunbc.live_deploy.apply::\{live_deploy_apply_desired_wet, live_deploy_apply_desired_operator_local_wet, live_deploy_apply_prod_role_wet, live_deploy_apply_prod_role_operator_wet, live_deploy_apply_prod_role_operator_local_wet, live_deploy_apply_prod_role_transaction_wet\}. Preserve their deployment/revision/access admission rather than creating store-selection authorities at each entry."),
    TableBlock {
      header: row(cells: [cell(text: "Configured workflow/deployment"), cell(text: "Current claim scope"), cell(text: "Boundary to preserve")]),
      alignments: [AlignNone, AlignNone, AlignNone],
      rows: [
        row(cells: [cell(text: "gunbc.live_deploy.desired::srv1_production_desired_deployment; srv1-live / srv1-daily-workspace"), cell(text: "Host-shared /opt/gunbc/attempt-state/worktree-claims"), cell(text: "The production role uses the transaction route selected by workflow fleet-converge, job dashboard-deploy, dispatch mode dashboard_deploy. This is a configured route, not a claim of live execution.")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "gunbc.live_deploy.desired::srv1_lab_desired_deployment; srv1-lab-codex-feedback-v0"), cell(text: "Instance-owned under srv1_dashboard_lab_root/attempt-state/worktree-claims"), cell(text: "Preserve lab isolation while deriving setup and use from the same instance.")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "gunbc.live_deploy.desired::srv2_deploy_desired_deployment; srv2-deploy"), cell(text: "Instance-owned under /home/briansrls/.local/share/gunbc-srv2-deploy/attempt-state/worktree-claims"), cell(text: "Preserve the declared service principal and the instance's state population.")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "Other public built-ins and supplied instances"), cell(text: "srv2 preview/lab and macbook-local are also public instance bindings; generic folds admit externally supplied instances."), cell(text: "The public roster is not all possible consumers. Workflow/repository owners must name external callers and actual rollout revisions before a production cut.")]),
      ],
    },
    p(text: "Claim reference is node_id plus attempt_key through worktree_claim_reference; the old store root additionally supplies the authority namespace. Metadata placement must not change the re-derived checkout path, local unit/capture evidence or authority to remove a tree. Linux service ownership and macOS briansrls:staff ownership remain their domain declarations; a shared logical store does not confer remote host cleanup authority."),
    h3(text: "C. Evidence that changes with the consumer"),
    TableBlock {
      header: row(cells: [cell(text: "Sites"), cell(text: "Migration or reuse"), cell(text: "Expected behavior and invariants")]),
      alignments: [AlignNone, AlignNone, AlignNone],
      rows: [
        row(cells: [cell(text: "test.claim.roadmap.attempt_worktree_claim_wet_witness::open_claim, pass, a_git_that_could_not_run_is_red_and_keeps_the_tree"), cell(text: "Replace the three direct raw-root entry calls and pre-created claim-directory fixture with an isolated fabric binding plus a real readiness-to-use route."), cell(text: "Retain the ten existing behavioral cases: crash gaps, live/dirty/unpushed/capture-pending trees, unclaimed/foreign trees, duplicates and unexecuted Git. Retain both-backend object controls; run claim/recovery controls on each backend admitted for that complete domain contract, with a remove-prerequisite negative control; directory repeat is Noop, duplicate record is not.")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "test.claim.roadmap.roadmap_dashboard_instance_witness::slot_store_roots_without_a_creator, every_slot_store_root_has_a_declared_creator, a_demand_list_without_the_claim_creator_leaves_that_root_uncreated"), cell(text: "Replace the claim-specific enrollment assertions with consumed fabric-readiness evidence, preserving the separate credential-store check."), cell(text: "A test must fail when real prerequisite production is removed; it must not require keeping the obsolete worktree-directory row merely to stay green.")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "test.claim.roadmap.belt_capture_intent_wet_witness::the_real_claim_adapters_observe_judge_and_remove_a_linked_worktree; test.claim.fabric.fabric_storage_file_store_wet_witness; test.claim.fabric_storage_r2_head; test.claim.fabric.fabric_storage_wire_witness"), cell(text: "Keep real Git/file adapters and provider/wire witnesses; extend only the boundaries changed by the migration."), cell(text: "Backend-independent records do not turn checkout removal into blob deletion. Real filesystem/Git observation and cleanup ordering remain exercised; supplied selection examples do not replace backend execution.")]),
      ],
    },
    h3(text: "D. Later adoption and shared-contract compatibility"),
    p(text: "The backend migrations in this group are later cohorts. Compatibility review of existing fabric callers is required in whichever delivery changes FabricPut or another public outcome; those callers are outside backend-migration scope, not outside that delivery's obligations."),
    TableBlock {
      header: row(cells: [cell(text: "Sites"), cell(text: "Migration or reuse"), cell(text: "Expected behavior and invariants")]),
      alignments: [AlignNone, AlignNone, AlignNone],
      rows: [
        row(cells: [cell(text: "gunbc.dispatch_credential_acquisition::credential_register_then_take, credential_open, credential_begin_launch, credential_admit_reader_or_discard, credential_discard_taken_attempt, credential_slot_record, credential_recover_root, credential_recover_slot, credential_terminate"), cell(text: "Replace slot-root plumbing/enrollment with a fabric binding. Entrances include roadmap_dispatch_actuator::dispatch_actuator_claude_selection_observed, cursor_selection_observed, selection_refused_discarding; roadmap_belt_actuate::belt_credential_admit_before_spawn, belt_snapshot_discarded_unless_consumed; roadmap_belt_tick_cli::belt_credential_recovery_cli."), cell(text: "Preserve durable registration before snapshot/runtime creation, transition ordering, confidentiality, CAS/history, enumeration and cgroup/reader evidence. credential_recover_slot currently takes path_parent_directory(root) as the local instance root: separate host cleanup context from the logical store. Credential bytes, Cursor runtime directories and the local recovery receipt are not automatically moved to R2.")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_session_placement::SessionPlacementStores, session_placement_stores, session_placement_acquire, session_placement_begin_launch, session_placement_abandon_at, session_placement_observe_at, session_placement_settle_pass_at; roadmap_session_activation_ensure::session_activation_ensure_pass_at"), cell(text: "Replace slots_root and its file-slot operations. Update belt_session_placement_for_container, belt_session_settlement_pass and their acquisition/activation/release paths; delete roadmap_belt_actuate::belt_session_slots_ensure after shared readiness owns it."), cell(text: "The current install -d -m 0700 uses implicit process ownership and exit status; shared readiness adds explicit owner/access checks and readback, so a foreign-owned root may refuse. Preserve slot-before-capacity-reservation, settlement-before-acquisition and no release on a lost close race. Keep the existing fabric capacity ledger, local placement records and exit spool distinct.")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "Other direct-file domain stores: gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_view_preference_store::issue_view_store_read, issue_view_store_commit; roadmap_dogfood_route::dogfood_start_record_for_instance, dogfood_route_acceptance_holds_on; gunbc.scm.repository_slot::read_repository_slot, publish_prepared; gunbc.serving.caller_backlog::persist_waiting_on_store, observe_durable_record, persist_derived_phase"), cell(text: "These verified file-call sites are later candidates for the same storage-interface adoption. Each needs its own caller and recovery inventory before migration."), cell(text: "Preserve per-principal namespaces, CAS conflicts, idempotent waits/resume behavior and existing retention. A common library does not establish that their durability/sharing requirements are identical.")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "Workspace commissioning: gunbc.workspace_commissioning_store::workspace_commissioning_store_observe, workspace_commissioning_publish_phase; workspace_commissioning_input_store::workspace_commissioning_input_read, workspace_commissioning_input_publish; workspace_commissioning_executor_store::workspace_executor_journal_observe, workspace_executor_journal_publish"), cell(text: "Later migrate their direct file journals after stating ownership/provenance and recovery obligations."), cell(text: "Keep commissioning admission, committed phase order and readback. Changing journal placement must not make an uncommissioned slot available or erase host-local custody obligations.")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "Approval/security state: gunbc.auth.approval_decision_store::observe_escalation, file_approval_request, commit_broker_decision, pending_escalations; approval_assertion_counter::observe_assertion_counter, assertion_counter_commit; approval_device_redemption::device_store_write, observe_enrolment_slot; gunbc.authorization_claim_slot::claim_authorization_slot, settle_authorization_claim; gunbc.host.host_boot_attempt_admission::consume_attempt_slot"), cell(text: "Later storage candidates, requiring security and history contracts at their own boundary. Approval-policy simplification remains a separate decision."), cell(text: "Preserve confidentiality, replay/monotonic counters, single consumption, enrollment/revocation and pending-request enumeration. Storage migration neither adds formal approval requests nor eliminates the sensitivity review.")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "Existing fabric result consumers: gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_task_store::roadmap_task_append; gunbc.harness.harness_seat::release_append; gunbc.spark.pair_serving_authority_log::placement_append, cancel_claimed_append, pair_serving_authority_establish, authority_transition_append; workspace_gateway_store::workspace_publish_gateway_at; workspace_allocation_store::workspace_commit_owner_transition; workspace_allocation_metrics::workspace_capture_runtime_metrics; workspace_allocation_milestones::workspace_record_first_ready; workspace_allocation_release::workspace_release_prepare; gunbc.live_deploy.tailnet_door_cutover_host::tailnet_door_cutover_journal_write"), cell(text: "These are conditional result-contract review sites if FabricPut or its projections change, not mandatory backend migrations. Also inspect workspace_acquisition_invocation::workspace_acquisition_actor_admits, workspace_cancel_unelected_actor, workspace_establish_actor_protocol and workspace_actor_slot_replace."), cell(text: "Each caller must explicitly handle or exclude any new outcome through its existing transaction/recovery law. The migration cannot assume that compiling the shared client proves its downstream callers still preserve behavior.")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "Already on fabric CAS: gunbc.workspace_allocation_store, workspace_gateway_store, workspace_acquisition_invocation, workspace_allocation_release, workspace_allocation_milestones, workspace_allocation_metrics; gunbc.live_deploy.tailnet_door_cutover_host"), cell(text: "Reuse these consumers as compatibility cases. They need result-handling or inferred-binding changes only if the shared interface changes, not a direct-file-to-fabric migration."), cell(text: "An import of file-store admission types is not a filesystem backend dependency. Preserve their existing operation semantics and authorization.")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "Exclusive holds: gunbc.fleet.printer_execution_hold::with_execution_hold; machine_intake.arrival_interlock::arrival_archive_slot_acquire, arrival_archive_slot_release; host.managed_host_unit_hold; workspace_slot_mutation; workspace_allocation_plan; fabric.fabric_cell_grant; fabric.fabric_control_plane"), cell(text: "Assess separately against durable-exclusive-hold/lease authorities. The file-CAS and hold realizations themselves remain backend implementations."), cell(text: "An ordinary object store is not a substitute for fencing, lease lifetime or exclusion. No automatic migration of these sites is included in the pilot.")]),
      ],
    },
    h3(text: "E. Closed source inventories for staffing"),
    p(text: "These populations are independently enumerated from tracked source at 7be4375e5a19. Direct file-CAS I/O has 25 non-test/non-instrument modules: 20 domain consumers, one lifecycle adapter and four implementations/providers. There are six immediate external lifecycle-I/O consumers, 16 file-hold callers/readers including two implementations/providers, and eight fabric-CAS modules including its implementation. These populations overlap; do not add the counts into a migration budget. The rosters name identities and dispositions so scope can be re-derived, rather than making a numeric count a gate."),
    TableBlock {
      header: row(cells: [cell(text: "Cohort"), cell(text: "Complete direct file-CAS module roster"), cell(text: "Direction and required behavior")]),
      alignments: [AlignNone, AlignNone, AlignNone],
      rows: [
