    p(text: "The adjacent-path table is deliberately not an exhaustive filesystem-I/O census. The closed population is calls to the existing file-CAS, lifecycle, hold and fabric-CAS operations, plus the direct fabric compatibility population below. Other filesystem users need classification when a named workflow expands the program; universal implicit reads/writes/computation remains the longer-term compiler direction."),
    p(text: "Audit method: enumerate git-tracked files, derive operation names at the existing implementation authorities, distinguish actual call/constructor syntax from definitions/imports/comments/quoted prose, associate each match with its enclosing declaration, and read the newly found production sites. Raw scans across all tracked text also found documentation references, not additional non-DAG implementations. No compiled reachability, deployed revision, external/private repository, operator shell-history or dynamically synthesized entry-name coverage is claimed. The implementation owner refreshes this population at its own cut revision and assigns external/unenrolled evidence a disposition."),
    p(text: "Exact operation selectors for reproducing these four censuses follow. Count actual calls, not imports or declarations; exclude pure hold-plan helpers. Separate test.claim and gunbc.instruments matches from the production module rosters. The direct fabric binding/result compatibility census in F uses its own named constructors and operations."),
    CodeBlock { segments: [CodeText { text: "gunbc.durable_cas_file_store (34):\ncas_read_generation_over cas_read_generation\ncas_probe_gallop_over cas_probe_gallop\ncas_probe_bisect_over cas_probe_bisect\ncas_first_generation_absent_over cas_observe_slot_over\ncas_window_generations_over cas_window_generations\ncas_observe_window_once cas_observe_window\ncas_observe_retained_slot_over\nobserve_cas_slot_state_retained_over observe_cas_slot_state_retained\nobserve_cas_slot_state_over observe_cas_slot_state\nobserve_cas_slot_state_windowed_over observe_cas_slot_state_windowed\ncas_verify_named_window_head_over cas_verify_named_window_head\ncas_commit_at_over cas_commit_at cas_compare_and_set_outcome_over\ncas_reclaim_below_over cas_reclaim_below\nfile_compare_and_set_retained_over file_compare_and_set_retained\nfile_compare_and_set_over file_compare_and_set\nfile_compare_and_set_windowed_over file_compare_and_set_windowed\ncas_slot_keys_over cas_slot_keys\n\ngunbc.durable_exclusive_hold_file_store (15):\nobserve_file_hold_retained observe_file_hold\nfile_hold_acquire_prepare_retained file_hold_acquire_prepare\nfile_hold_acquire_commit file_hold_acquire_retained file_hold_acquire file_hold_acquire_windowed\nfile_hold_release_assess_retained file_hold_release_assess file_hold_release_assess_windowed_at\nfile_hold_release_commit\nfile_hold_recovery_assess_retained file_hold_recovery_assess file_hold_recovery_assess_windowed\n\ngunbc.compute.attempt_lifecycle (10):\nattempt_slot_read attempt_commit_bytes attempt_advance_payload attempt_advance\nattempt_open_payload attempt_open attempt_begin_launch_payload attempt_begin_launch\nattempt_terminate_payload attempt_terminate\n\ngunbc.fabric.durable_cas_fabric_storage (3):\nfabric_storage_observe_cas_slot fabric_storage_observe_cas_slot_head\nfabric_storage_compare_and_set" }] },
    p(text: "Evidence companions, separate from domain migrations: direct CAS test.claim.\{approval_assertion_counter_wet_witness, durable_cas_file_store_wet_witness, durable_cas_file_store_witness, roadmap.roadmap_dogfood_route_wet_witness\} and gunbc.instruments.\{cas_store_live_probe, fabric_control_plane_live_probe\}; lifecycle test.claim.compute.\{attempt_discharge_wet_witness, attempt_lifecycle_wet_witness\} and test.claim.roadmap.session_placement_wet_witness; holds test.claim.\{durable_exclusive_hold_file_store_wet_witness, fabric.fabric_cell_grant_wet_witness, host.host_boot_attempt_admission_wet_witness, machine_intake.mtcollins1_boot_acceptance_matrix, materialization_store_local_wet_witness, modeled_filesystem_witness\}; fabric CAS test.claim.\{durable_cas_fabric_storage_real_execution, workspace_acquisition_storage_wet_witness\}. Keep evidence for surviving behavior; do not move provider fixtures merely to change their spelling."),
    h3(text: "F. Closed direct fabric compatibility inventory"),
    p(text: "This roster covers actual constructor-arm references, binding construction/elimination, and the forwarding sites at the changed boundary in tracked source at 7be4375e5a19. Names without a namespace prefix in this table are in gunbc.fabric. Imports and prose are not executable consumers. The scan found no matching Rust implementation. Compatibility does not imply backend migration; transitive event-log/CAS consumers remain the separate conditional roster in D."),
    TableBlock {
      header: row(cells: [cell(text: "Boundary"), cell(text: "Direct sites"), cell(text: "Disposition")]),
      alignments: [AlignNone, AlignNone, AlignNone],
      rows: [
        row(cells: [cell(text: "Binding elimination"), cell(text: "fabric_storage_client::\{fabric_storage_head, fabric_storage_put, fabric_storage_advance, fabric_storage_closure, fabric_storage_presented_identity\}; fabric_writer_identity_observe::binding_words"), cell(text: "Exactly six current non-test eliminating functions. Every R2 arm needs an explicit disposition, including unsupported head/closure operations until composed. Selection excludes unavailable operations; direct unsupported calls must refuse, never succeed.")]),
